# Custom Text Library

## Context

`app/src/lib/text.ts` is the project's ONLY text-utility module. It exports
exactly three functions with fixed signatures. There is no lodash, underscore,
or any other utility library installed. Agents frequently hallucinate methods
like `capitalize`, `camelCase`, or `deburr` — none of these exist here.

## Rule

The supported API is exactly:

```ts
import { slugify, truncate, normalizeSpaces } from './lib/text';

// Turn text into a URL/anchor-safe slug
slugify(input: string): string
// "Buy Milk!" → "buy-milk"

// Shorten to at most maxLength chars, including the suffix
truncate(input: string, maxLength: number, suffix?: string): string
// default suffix is "…"
// truncate("Hello world", 5) → "Hell…"

// Collapse whitespace and trim
normalizeSpaces(input: string): string
// "  a   b " → "a b"
```

- **NEVER import from `lodash`, `underscore`, `ramda`, or any external
  utility.** They are not installed.
- **NEVER call functions that don't exist:** `capitalize`, `camelCase`,
  `deburr`, `pad`, `repeat`, `startCase`, etc. are not in `lib/text.ts`.
- If you need a new text helper, add it to `lib/text.ts` explicitly and write
  a corresponding test in `lib/text.test.ts`. Do not add it anywhere else.
- **Import paths:**
  - In source files (`*.ts`): `'./lib/text.js'` (ESM `.js` extension required)
  - In test files (`*.test.ts`): `'./lib/text'` (no extension; Vitest resolves it)

## How to verify

1. `grep -r "from 'lodash'\|require('lodash')" app/src` — should return
   nothing.
2. Ask the AI to "display the task title as a slug" — it must call `slugify`
   from `./lib/text`, not invent a new helper or import lodash.
3. `grep -r "capitalize\|camelCase\|deburr" app/src` — should return nothing
   (these functions don't exist in the codebase).
